---
/**
 * privacy.astro — the privacy policy (D-289; updated 2026-09-10 for
 * Cloudflare Web Analytics, D-293).
 *
 * What it is: an honest description of the two real things this site does
 * with visitor data — the beta signup form, and Cloudflare's own cookieless
 * Web Analytics beacon — written to match what actually runs, not a generic
 * template. Cross-checked against src/data/beta.ts, BETA_SIGNUP_SETUP.md, and
 * (as of D-293) Base.astro's own third-party script tag before writing a word
 * of it.
 * What it does NOT do: claim a cookie policy or a GDPR/CCPA compliance
 * certification this site hasn't earned, or describe a cookie-consent banner
 * for cookies that do not exist (Web Analytics is cookieless by design — see
 * the "Cookies and tracking" section for what that does and does not mean).
 * This page originally said "no analytics anywhere" — true when D-289 wrote
 * it, false once Cloudflare auto-enabled Web Analytics on this zone; found
 * live via a Lighthouse trace, and fixed here rather than left to drift, per
 * this whole site's own discipline (docs/08-decisions.md, D-264) against
 * fabricated-for-appearances content — including a claim that quietly stops
 * being true.
 * This is a good-faith, factually-grounded draft, not legal advice — see
 * the note at the bottom of the page and in this repo's own decision log
 * (D-289, D-293) for what a real legal review should still check.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';

const updated = 'September 10, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Apelles"
  description="What Apelles's website collects: an email, only if you request beta access, plus cookieless aggregate visit stats. Never sold, no cookies."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lede={`Last updated ${updated}. Short version: the only thing you give us is an email address, only if you ask for beta access — plus cookieless, anonymous visit stats every page load sends automatically.`}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the "Request beta access" form (on the home page, or the one in the hero), we
        collect the email address you type in, and — only if you choose to answer it — what you
        make, from a fixed list of options. Nothing else on this site asks you for anything.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do with it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your email address for exactly one purpose: to tell you when there is a build of
        Apelles worth installing. That is the one email the signup copy promises, and it is the
        only one you will get from us. We do not sell it, rent it, or share it with anyone for
        marketing. We do not build a mailing list beyond this one purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Who actually receives it</h2>
      <p>
        The form posts directly to <a class="link" href="https://formsubmit.co">FormSubmit.co</a>,
        a third-party form-processing service, which forwards the submission by email to the
        project owner's inbox. FormSubmit is the only third party your email address passes
        through — read <a class="link" href="https://formsubmit.co/privacy-policy">FormSubmit's
        own privacy policy</a> for how they handle it on their end before it reaches us. We do not
        use a mailing-list platform, a CRM, or any analytics tool to process it further.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies of its own, and runs one analytics script:
        <a class="link" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web
        Analytics</a>, which the site's own infrastructure host enables automatically for any site
        it hosts. It is built specifically to avoid the things a cookie banner exists to gate: no
        cookies, no browser storage, and — per Cloudflare's own design for this product — no
        fingerprinting or persistent identifier used to recognise you across visits or other sites.
        What it does send, on every page load, is aggregate, anonymous traffic data (which pages get
        visited, roughly how fast they load, in what country and browser) that cannot be tied back
        to you individually. Read
        <a class="link" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's own privacy
        policy</a> for exactly what it collects and how. Because none of this identifies you or
        persists across visits, it doesn't trigger a cookie-consent requirement, so this page still
        has no cookie banner — a banner gating consent for tracking that isn't the identifying kind
        would be exactly the kind of decoration this site tries not to ship. This is the one thing
        that changed since this page was first written (found live, via a Lighthouse trace, not
        assumed); if the site's own behaviour changes again, this page changes with it, in the same
        commit.
      </p>
      <p>
        One narrow exception, for transparency: a development-only tool used while building this
        site (a position-tuning panel for the home page's hero image) writes a few numeric values
        to your browser's own <code class="mono">localStorage</code> if you happen to load the site
        while it is running in development mode. That tool is compiled out of the production build
        entirely — it does not exist in the site you are reading this on.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Until we send you the one email the signup promises, or until you ask us to delete your
        address sooner, whichever comes first. We do not have an automated deletion schedule beyond
        that; if you want your address removed at any time, contact us (below) and we will remove it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Don't want to be contacted? Don't use the form. Nothing else on this site asks for anything.</li>
        <li>Want your address deleted? Email us and we will remove it.</li>
        <li>Want to know exactly what we hold? Ask — it is one email address and, optionally, one word describing what you make.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For anything on this page — a deletion request, a question about what we hold — email
        <a class="link" href="mailto:ashish.1999vns@gmail.com">ashish.1999vns@gmail.com</a>, the
        same inbox the beta signup form already delivers to.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        If what this site actually collects or does with it changes, this page changes in the same
        commit — that is a standing rule for this whole codebase (see this repo's own
        <code class="mono">CLAUDE.md</code>), not a promise made separately from the code.
      </p>

      <p class="fine">
        This page is a good-faith, factually accurate description of what this site's own code
        does, written and checked against that code rather than assumed — it is not a substitute
        for legal advice, and has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Before relying on it for a real
        public launch, especially for visitors in the EU (GDPR) or California (CCPA), have it
        reviewed by one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prose .link {
    color: var(--pigment-terracotta);
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--pigment-terracotta) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .prose .link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--pigment-terracotta);
  }

  .plain {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .plain li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .fine {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--edge);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
  }
</style>
